body who works with  him is fortunate  alongside crews the only other top gun  actor we know is returning for the  sequel is val kilmer who played  maverick's rival and would-be wingman  tom iceman kazansky however there's  already a fan theory that suggests that  iceman is going to die in the sequel in  footage released so far we see maverick  attending a funeral which definitely  means that someone's going down the fact  that kilmer's character failed to appear  in any of the trailers implies to  pessimistic fans that it has to be  iceman in the coffin regardless of his  character's potential fate it'll be good  to see kilmer back on screen the actor  has been largely out of the public eye  in recent years after spending two years  between 2015 and 2017 battling throat  cancer with an operation on his trachea  affecting his voice and leaving him  short of breath in 2021 a documentary  revealed that he now talks with the help  of an electronic device prior to the  release of that documentary kilmer  expressed excitement for top gun  maverick telling the hollywood reporter  in 2019 it will be a great film i  promise this time around had me laughing  with tom like a high schooler he's so  funny i hope he saved the world enough  to take a decade and re-establish  himself as a great comedian as he has it  in him  while miles teller ultimately emerged  victorious in the dogfight for the major  role of bradley bradshaw another  contender was granted a pretty  impressive consolation prize you may  know up-and-comer glenn powell's face  from a small but important role as  astronaut john glenn in hidden figures  or from the richard linklater directed  everybody wants some he's most recently  been finding fans as a romantic lead in  the netflix original movies set it up  and the guernsey literary and potato  peel pie society after it was confirmed  that teller would play bradshaw on the  top gun sequel powell joked on twitter  i'm taking down all the tom cruise  posters in my bedroom maybe i'll leave  one two for symmetry okay the posters  are stained however he quickly found a  reason to keep those posters up as part  of his audition process powell had flown  to cruz's home in clearwater florida the  movie's producers including crews  decided that they liked pals so much  that they would be casting him in a  different role and even beefing it up  for him his appearance in the trailer  has already made an impression  what do we have here yeah here i thought  we were special  some viewers may recognize jay ellis as  a clueless tech bro lawrence on hbo's  insecure but top gun maverick brings the  actor slightly closer to his roots since  ellis grew up in a military family  however as he made clear to jimmy kimmel  in 2018 his family were air force not  navy like the fighter pilots in the film  he explained i called him and i said hey  i booked up gun he goes oh man  it's the navy right  and i was like yeah but it's also top  gun he's like that's cool  ellis who appears to be playing a young  recruit also gushed over working with  tom cruise he said he has this ability  to look you in the eye and make you feel  like you're the prettiest girl in the  room nicest most genuine giving open guy  i've never worked with anyone who's like  listen if you need anything truly pick  up the phone and call i'm going to show  you every single thing i know it's  really amazing a few months later he  echoed ham and connolly's predictions  for the audience's reactions telling  entertainment tonight that top gun  maverick was going to blow people's  minds  depending on your tv preferences you may  know monica barbaro from season 2 of  unreal a dark comedy about the making of  a fictional reality tv show or from  criminal justice series like chicago pd  chicago justice or the good cop if you  don't recognize her consider this her  breakout moment in august 2018 variety  reported that barbaro would be playing a  fighter pilot with a callsign phoenix a  love interest to teller's character from  the trailers she looks like one of many  new members to this batch of ace top gun  pilots alongside charles parnell bashir  salahuddin and danny ramirez  as with every tom cruise movie these  days details on the plot of top gun  maverick are being held close to the  vast at comic con cruz limited his  comments saying simply top gun is about  family about sacrifice and it's about  aviation all of which frankly we could  have guessed however we have got a few  tidbits of the story to work with first  of all there is a strong implication  that maverick's persistent daredevil  antics are putting him behind the times  in the trailer ed harris's rear admiral  tells him the end is inevitable maverick  you kind of set it for extinction  further reports suggest that the plot  revolves around the captain's role as a  mentor to the new recruits as he tries  to come to terms with technical advances  like drones that could make skill sets  and attitudes like his obsolete  additionally per the film's official  synopsis maverick is drawn into a  confrontation with his own deepest fears  culminating in a mission that demands  the ultimate sacrifice from those who  will be chosen to fly it however before  you worry that we're going to see people  with remote controls instead of cockpit  controls director joseph kozinski has  already quashed rumors that drones will  play a big role in 2017 he told  cinemablend personally i would never  want to see a movie about drones for me  top gun has always been about fighter  planes it's been about fighter pilots  the second maverick trailer landed on  december 16 2019 and in addition to more  shots of incredible stunts it brought  fresh clues about the potential plots  and some of the characters the voiceover  confirms that maverick is returning as  an instructor and while we aren't told  where he's been a scene at the end  implies that he's been working as a test  pilot we also get more clarity on some  of his pupils the call sign of monica  barbaro's character is phoenix danny  ramirez is fanboy and miles tellers  bradley bradshaw is rooster a suitably  bird-related tribute to the character's  father hopefully rooster's flying  attempts are more successful than his  namesakes were the trailer also nods at  goose's fate in a few more moments when  the voice over says that maverick's  lessons could be the difference between  life and death we cut to rooster clearly  with his father on his mind rooster also  starts a fight in a classroom so it's  clear that the character has some  pent-up emotions to wrestle with and the  moment in the trailer when a jet loses  one of its engines is a clear callback  to goose's death speaking of emotions  the trailer confirms another plot point  that the first teaser hinted at we know  that a character who served in the navy  dies thanks to an extended view of the  funeral it's not a whole lot more to go  on but it's got us feeling the need for  a sequel with maverick inspired levels  of impatience  after months of keeping all things top  gun 2 top secret in january 2022  director joseph kaczynski teased more of  the plot shared some photos and  confirmed the new pilot's names fellas  this here's bagman hangman whatever  in addition to tellers rooster barbaros  phoenix and ramirez's fanboy glenn  powell's character's call sign is  hangman jay ellis is playing payback and  lewis pullman is bob  the director told entertainment weekly  that this batch of young pilots have  already graduated from top gun and are  returning to school for a special  training detachment they're at a higher  level than the students in the first  film which means more impressive  maneuvers for the audience and truly  terrifying training for the actors  kaczynski revealed that cruz himself  designed an aerial training course to  prepare them when they were ready the  team rigged six imax quality cameras in  the cockpit of each actor's f-18 super  hornet capture them as they pretended to  fly the plane the real job was actually  left to a navy pilot as crews found on  the first film being tossed around like  this takes a physical toll kaczynski  admitted that some of the actors  occasionally threw up away from the  action he offered one other insight into  the movie story rooster and maverick's  relationship is the film's emotional  core fly all the planes you want but no  amount of preparation will get you ready  to relive the emotional swings of  maverick and goose  although the costumes from top gun are  some of the most iconic in hollywood  history one of the film's most famous  and enduring scenes involved very few  clothes that would be the scene showing  the pilots blowing off steam with a game  of shirtless volleyball in the  documentary danger zone the making of  top gun director tony scott joked about  the scene reminiscing about the time  that he got the guys to get all their  gear off to get sprayed down with baby  oil even decades later the scene is a  topic of discussion and parody that even  the movie's director has a hard time  taking seriously i didn't have a vision  about what i was doing other than just  doing  soft porn  with all this in mind it makes sense  that the top gun maverick promos would  promise us a return to the volleyball  court or maybe this time the football  field in the sequel's first trailer we  see glenn powell's character shirtless  and silhouetted against the sun spinning  a football on his finger before cutting  to a scene of him mimicking slider's  roar from the original movie so even if  the sport has changed it looks like  there's still time for fun and games at  top gun  let's talk about some jacket controversy  maverick's classic fur collared leather  aviator jacket became an icon in its own  right after the first movie so you'd  think fans would be pleased to see an  old friend returning for the trailer  however the jacket's appearance caused a  stir among eagle-eyed viewers thanks to  the patches on the back in the original  top gun the patch on the back of the  jacket bears four rectangles including  the taiwanese flag and the japanese flag  in the trailer for top gun maverick when  maverick puts on the jacket these flags  have been replaced with two similar  looking designs in the same color  schemes so what's the big deal some fans  suggested that this was a political  decision and not a costuming one top gun  maverick is partly funded by chinese  internet company tencent china has a  tense history with japan and doesn't  recognize taiwan as independent so it  may be that tencent wasn't big on seeing  a portrayal of an alliance between those  two countries and the u.s navy however  at least one former naval pilot ward  carroll has dismissed the suggestion  pointing out via twitter that the top  gun patches are notoriously haphazard  anyway meaning that this latest  alteration could just be for looks  in top gun maverick there is no hot air  around those stunts as tom cruise  assured his comic con audience  and everything you see in this film  obviously it's it's for real  jon hamm echoed the assertion telling  people the aerial footage is  mind-blowing and it's mostly practical  there's not a lot of cg those guys are  really up in planes and getting thrown  around in multiple g's and it wasn't  just the planes jennifer connolly said  that she and cruz really rode maverick's  motorcycle she said he's an excellent  excellent motorcyclist i have to say  every single time he stops exactly on  the mark like an inch from the curb very  skilled just as cruz learned to fly in  the f-14s he made sure the rest of the  cast could handle the impact for  themselves he told conan o'brien we  hired  incredible actors great cast brilliant  and then but they also had to be able to  fly in the airplane  so we had to train them  crews said all the actors were tested to  see if they could handle the g-forces at  fighter pilots experience plus the crew  had to train the fighter pilots who were  really flying the planes about  filmmaking techniques  getting to the rank of captain in the  u.s navy is nothing to sneeze at as cruz  himself pointed out we're working with  the navy i mean incredible pilots  greatest fighter pilots in the world  and yet over 30 years into his  distinguished service why maverick is  still not a higher rank is not just a  question that's troubling ed harris's  rear admiral  you should be at least a two-star  admiral by now  yet here you are  captain  it's something real-life naval officers  have wondered too luckily one stepped in  to answer according to navy personnel  command there are three reasons why  maverick could still be a captain the  first and probably least likely is that  he started out as an enlisted and thus  not in the officer branch that leads to  the higher ranks the first movie kind of  disproves this though since he was a  lieutenant in 1986 he could also  technically have retired but been  retained something that rarely happens  and which runs counter to the rear  admiral statement that maverick won't  retire the most likely thing is that he  could have taken some time off perhaps  after goose's death a break in service  could mean forfeiting promotion or it  could just be that he really likes a  hands-on job of flying planes more than  he wants to be a well-paid manager we  may get our answer when the movie comes  out or it could just remain one of  life's mysteries  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

